  "scope": "Functional exact post-validation capability rebinding at raw execution. Whole execution success derives successful re-extraction of the token item through actual comparison, before dispatching projected action effects in the token context. Extraction/mismatch preserve input cache. Bound Ordinary late-volume conflict retains earlier raw cache; cryptography, extractor internals, native controls, atomic evidence refresh and full Transfer remain open. Whole wrapper execution success derives successful extraction of exactly the token item in its context through the executable equality check; no desired exactMatched boolean is a premise. Extraction failure and unequal complete item retain the input cache and precede all raw effects. Exact successful rebinding dispatches projections of the same captured action with Ordinary/FeeFunding from the token context. Actual verified-token provenance, extractor internals, real Verification equality/bytes and Item-to-effect semantic projection remain interfaces. Bound Ordinary current volume conflict derives the raw error retaining the earlier cache. The first compiler-zero warning output is rejected as a whole and adds no proof or negative-control credit.",
